Expanded story:
Amy stirred a pot of oatmeal on the stove while Will and Amber giggled over their cereal bowls in the sunny kitchen; a sudden groan from outside rattled the windows as a zombie burst through the front door, shuffling toward her with its empty eyes. She grabbed the two kids by their shoulders and shoved them into the back bedroom’s closet, slamming the heavy door behind them before sprinting back to the kitchen where she could hear the zombie’s clumsy footsteps echoing down the hallway. Amy slipped a pistol from a hollowed-out space in the fridge wall and pulled out a gleaming katana that had been tucked beneath her cutting board all morning. She fired at the approaching creature, its head snapping off with a wet thud; then she swung the sword, slicing another zombie’s torso cleanly as it staggered back toward the doorway. More zombies surged in through cracks around the doorframe—one lunging for Will, another swiping at Amber—but Amy kept her pistol and katana poised, firing one after another until each groaning victim fell with a splash of blood onto the kitchen tiles. Even as the last zombie collapsed, a fresh pair emerged from the hallway’s shadow, but she met them head‑on, blasting their heads off before they could reach the closet door. The final zombie lay still on the floorboards; Amy wiped her palm on her jeans and turned toward the back bedroom where Will and Amber waited in silent relief. She opened the closet door wide and pulled the two kids out into the kitchen’s bright light, holding them close as she stepped forward to face whatever more undead might come.
